/.bsp/
/null/
/.idea/

# `project/` is BUILD SOURCE and must be committed: `project/plugins.sbt` supplies every
# symbol build.sbt uses from a plugin (dynverVTagPrefix, idePackagePrefix, MdocPlugin,
# ScalaUnidocPlugin, mimaPreviousArtifacts, ProblemFilters, sonatypeCredentialHost, mdocIn)
# and `project/build.properties` pins sbt itself to 1.10.11.  Without them a fresh clone
# cannot even load the build.
#
# This file used to ignore `/project/` wholesale.  That was harmless only by accident: the two
# source files were tracked *before* the rule was added, and a gitignore entry does not affect
# an already-tracked file.  Any NEW file there -- the `project/Dependencies.scala` that a
# growing build eventually wants -- would have been silently untracked, and the breakage would
# have surfaced as a failing CI run on someone else's clone rather than here.
#
# Only the build OUTPUT under project/ is ignored, and the unanchored `target/` below already
# covers `project/target/` and `project/project/target/`.
project/project/
# UNANCHORED since the 5.2 phase 1.1 module split: the leading slash matched the root
# target/ only, so core/target/ and repl/target/ -- and any future module's -- would have
# been committed. Matches a directory named `target` at any depth, the sbt convention.
target/

# Jekyll documentation-site build artifacts (see .github/workflows/pages.yml)
/_site/
/docs/_site/
/docs/.jekyll-cache/
/docs/Gemfile.lock

/CLAUDE.md
/.sbtopts
/ToDo.md
/DesignNotes.md
